{
	"_doc": "Procedural enemy ships (scripts/space/shipgen.gd, docs/CONTENT.md sections 4c, 14 and 18). An enemy is built from (faction, size class, seed, budget). budget: the budget of a fight = tier_base[tier] x (1 + per_jump x jumps) x the region's danger x the difficulty; stage_mult: the run stages (1 to 8) that fight with a share of that budget (stages 1 to 3: 70%, Beta 3; the later ones and 0 = unknown: all of it); shield_cap: the most likely an enemy of that stage is to carry a shield at all (25%, 40%, 55%; rolled from the ship's seed in Shipgen.build, the rare factions ignore it; the spec says the stage with a trailing `:s<stage>`); size_from: the budget from which a ship is medium or large (size_jitter blurs the line, +- that fraction, by the seed). A region is not here: its data file (data/regions/*.json) says its `danger` and its `enemies`, the faction whose table the pirates of the region are built from (Shipgen.faction_for). sizes: per size class the nominal hull `width` (outer, cells), `k_mid` (the decks between the gun deck and the engine room), `max_interior` (the widest deck's floor) and `max`, the most of each thing the hull holds (bow = weapons on the bow; flank = turrets on the flanks; engine, reactor, shield; armour = layers; crew; beds). factions: per faction, `line` (its usual equipment line), `name_pool` (names.json), `crew` (species, names), `ai` (aim_skill from..to, rammer = chance of a ram bowed rammer when the seed decides, morale = the style of data/morale.json it breaks in; a rammer is always the ram style), `weights` (what the faction spends its budget on: weapons, armour, shield, engine, crew, skill, systems), `armour` (the plating tile of each layer, outermost first, and each tile's cost factor), `layer_cost` (the cost of one layer of armour per size class), `parts` (what it buys: the free part of each kind `base`, then `weapons`, `shields`, `engines`, `reactors`, `systems`: {id, cost, weight, from (the least budget at which it is for sale), needs (parts that come with it)}), and `hull`, the silhouette grammar (scripts/space/hullgen.gd): `prow` and `tail` the extra floor rows (min, max) behind the guns and before the engines, which lengthen the narrow ends; `band` the share of the widest deck each deck gets (gun, bridge, core, aux, engine), `jitter_w` extra floor width per deck (min, max), `jitter_c` how far a deck's centre may slip, `asym` (true: left and right edges are rolled apart), `ops` the shaping steps in order: wedge (fills a step with a slope), chamfer (cuts a corner), spikes (saw teeth on a flank), arc (round2 corner). threat: how enemy_power / player_power is turned into 1-5 skulls (`cuts` are the ratios where it goes up a skull) and the constants of the power estimate (kinetic_floor: a kinetic gun's hit counts over this much damage when it is smaller, see threat.gd). Costs are in budget units.",
